# gradlew runs on the Linux CI runner. If it is ever committed with CRLF endings the
# shebang breaks and the runner reports "bad interpreter", which is the same class of
# Windows-only failure as the missing executable bit that broke the first release.
# Scoped deliberately: a repo-wide `* text=auto` would renormalise every file and bury
# the next real diff in churn.
gradlew text eol=lf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf

*.jar binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
